# `assets/figures/` — Non-regenerable authored figures

## Authority

The root [`README.md`](../../README.md) contract defines this as the source home
for figures that code cannot recreate.

## Use this directory for

Create one folder per authored figure, `assets/figures/<slug>/`, containing:

- the editable source when export is possible (`.svg`, `.ai`, or equivalent);
- any canonical raster/PDF export used by the pipeline or reporting; and
- `source.yaml` (or a README) naming the title, creator, creation date, authoring
  tool, editable source, exports, external source/license when applicable, and
  notes needed to edit it safely.

Files at or below the repository's 1 MiB Git limit may be committed directly.
Store larger or frequently changing binary assets with {{ data_versioning }} at
the same logical path and commit the pointer. This template does not promise Git
LFS support.

## Do not put here

- A data-derived plot → `results/figures/`.
- A programmatically assembled composite → `results/figures/`.
- A one-time copy of a figure sent externally → the artifact's immutable
  `reporting/.../deliveries/` directory.

A manually assembled composite is an authored asset and belongs here; record
that non-regenerable choice in its source metadata.
